            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "KRICKYR"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Excellent recipe. I hesitated to purchase the huge jar of tahini at $5+, but now have confidence that it will get used up just from this recipe alone. I only added about 3 tablespoons fresh lemon juice, and it's perfect. By the way, garbanzo beans and chickpeas are the same thing."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "lisa4517"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great recipe. I roasted my own red peppers (2 of them) and used them. (@425; rotating so all sides are roasted and skin is peeling and browned)",
            "datePublished": "2014-04-15T18:00:22.847Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "TBowerman"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Roasted Red pepper hummus. This is a very easy recipe. The hardest part was peeling the roasted bell peppers. The recipe did not include a portion of plain yogurt or plain sour cream or anything like that to make it even more creamy. It needs the sour cream or the yogurt to bring a little tang and extra creaminess to the hummus. Suggest adding equal parts yogurt to tahini to the blender while making at start. Add more to taste. Also added a quarter cup of extra virgin olive oil. For that reason, you give a four star.",
            "datePublished": "2019-05-02T21:00:26.340Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Robert P"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Perfect blend. I roasted the bell pepper on the gas range and that made a difference to the flavor. Fresh lemon and garlic.... this is a keeper. Will make this a lot.",
            "datePublished": "2020-10-25T18:18:02.177Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Alan"
            },
            "reviewBody": "We made a few changes, but stuck to the core recipe.\n\n5 cloves garlic (this is a garlic-loving house!)\nFresh basil (~6 leaves), since we had some on hand\n3/4 c. roasted red pepper\n1/4 c. lemon juice\n1/8 c. water (wanted the zing of the lemon juice, but not as much; used water to reach the right consistency)",
            "datePublished": "2019-06-09T18:16:04.343Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Ireland Wetnight"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe was a good foundation for hummus; however, I recommend adding only 1-2 teaspoons of lemon juice instead of a third of a cup. Otherwise, the lemon taste is very overpowering and sour. \n\nAlso, you might add some cumin for more flavor.",
            "datePublished": "2020-01-11T19:53:33.993Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Em"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very easy and delicious! I used 3 garlic cloves, 1 cup of peppers, and added a couple tablespoons of EVOO. Thank you!",
            "datePublished": "2014-02-02T05:40:48.110Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jill Danielson"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Added extra ground black pepper and salt to taste, cummin (approx. 1/4 tsp), crushed red pepper flakes (approx. 1/2 tsp), and juice from 1 lime.",
            "datePublished": "2015-06-08T19:21:24.730Z"
