            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "rhamm"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Cooking my own garbanzo beans definitely punched up the flavor. I just soak dried beans for 8 hours )or up to 24 hours), and cook them with lots of herbs - basil, bay leaf, garlic - to make things a bit more interesting. Having fresh lemon juice makes a big difference as well.",
            "datePublished": "2013-03-11T16:14:39.647Z"
          },
          {
