            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jo-Anne Beckett"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I followed the recipe exactly, using chick peas that I cooked myself (superior in taste). I used store bought jarred roasted red peppers (my reason for making the recipe. This is delicious. No oil was needed.",
            "datePublished": "2025-01-20T10:48:23.586Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Pam"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I found it needed more tahini. With that, it still didn't taste like the hummus I'm used to eating (usually from a supermarket). Regardless, it was still very tasty, and all my guests ate it up, too. I came to the conclusion that it didn't taste like store bought because all of the ingredients, less the tahini and chickpeas, were fresh and the final product wasn't \"enhanced\" by preservatives.",
            "datePublished": "2024-09-30T18:59:42.277Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Stacey"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Easy to make! I agree with other reviewers on the olive oilI as a constant character in hummus recipes. I added evoo, tad of water and a dash of paprika. I also roasted my own red peppers.",
            "datePublished": "2024-07-09T23:56:16.399Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "2"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Linda Rich"
            },
            "reviewBody": "One major ingredient that was left out.....EXTRA VIRGIN OLIVE OIL. The ingredients wouldn't budge in my blender unless I added either water or EVO. I never heard or made any hummus recipe that didn't have EVO. While it does taste good, I'm not sure if I would use this recipe again.",
            "datePublished": "2024-06-29T14:05:27.496Z"
